WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.872
- So, President Biden rescinded
the Trump executive orders

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:05.840
that basically sought
to ban TikTok and WeChat

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:06.941
in the United States, which,

00:00:06.941 --> 00:00:08.260
if you're watching this,

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.080
that probably would
have affected your life.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.960
So the thing is, the
Trump executive orders

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.170
never went into effect.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.700
Judges in multiple lawsuits
had issued injunctions

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.100
that prevented those executive orders

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.070
from going into effect.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.810
And basically, those executive orders

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.110
were sort of unworkable,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.478
because they singled
out specific companies.

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:25.931
But TikTok and WeChat
are not out of the woods.

00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:28.130
Replacing the Trump executive orders

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.330
are the Biden executive orders

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.260
that don't single out
a particular company,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.500
but instead purport to look at

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.440
the national security interest
related to all these apps.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.210
So, if they are harvesting data

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.213
for national security issues,

00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:39.301
potentially they might still be shut down

00:00:39.301 --> 00:00:41.350
even under the Biden administration.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.953
So, we'll probably see TikTok in court.

